   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to directing the New York State Department of Labor to\nestablish a voluntary training and certification program for employers\nentitled the Neurodiversity Training Pledge",
    "basePrintNo": "S4593",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4593-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 15,
       "fullName": "Joseph P. Addabbo Jr.",
       "imgName": "384_joseph_p._addabbo_jr.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 384,
       "sessionMemberId": 2332,
       "sessionYear": 2025,
       "shortName": "ADDABBO"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Labor",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4593\n\nSPONSOR: FAHY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to directing the New York State Department of Labor\nto establish a voluntary training and certification program for employ-\ners entitled the Neurodiversity Training Pledge\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to directing the New York State Department of Labor to establish\na voluntary training and certification program for employers that have\ntaken the Neurodiversity Training Pledge.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 subdivision (a): Directs the New York State Department of\nLabor to establish a voluntary training and certification program for\nemployers that have taken the Neurodiversity Pledge.\n\nSection 1 subdivision (b): Directs the Department of Labor to develop\nand manage the program and establishes the key components and topics to\nbe included in the training program.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nB-print amendments provide technical changes and specify that certif-\nication would be awarded to the employer following completion of the\ntraining program. The amendments also allow the Department of Labor to\nconsult with other groups as deemed necessary in the development of the\nprogram.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nRecently new laws have been enacted and initiatives launched to improve\nthe lives of New Yorkers with disabilities and to enhance their-employ-\nment opportunities. Both the public and private sector are engaged in\nthese efforts. The success of implementation of these laws and initi-\natives depend in large measure upon neurodiversity training and neurodi-\nverse workforce hiring.\n\nThe Department of Labor is well-positioned to lead a voluntary program\nfor businesses that pledge to undertake-neurodiversity training for\ntheir employees and adopt best practices for a neurodiverse workforce.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-2024 A9131 (Burdick) - reported referred to Rules\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
